37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: The invoices confirm my fear. Separately licensed pieces climbed yearly, while bundled agreements held steady.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: The outage report is brutal. Four suppliers, zero ownership, and two days of chaos. That’s exactly the gap I feared.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: The dispatch tool skipped three upgrades. We are running on 2012 hardware, and the 2018 data lift left a year of errors.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: The administrator data is alarming. Two key people retire this year, and the last hiring took eleven months. We are critically understaffed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: The yard devices are a mess of old models, and the 2021 trial failed fast. We need a system that works with what we actually have.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Toshio, the board minutes show capital requests trimmed for three years, while operating lines passed easily. We are structurally locked into recurring costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Yumi, that unowned outage is exactly why I’m worried. If the plan drifts, who actually answers when the lights go out?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Benjamin, the 2018 data lift confirms my suspicion. External work came back broken, and we spent a year fixing it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,- **Misaki**: The supervisor findings are worse. Standard steps were dropped within weeks. We cannot rely on training alone to fix this.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: The calendar is the real killer. No freeze window in winter means any cutover risks total chaos.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Toshio, the board minutes show capital requests trimmed for three years, while operating lines passed easily. We are structurally locked into recurring costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Yumi, exactly. The scope froze at start, then broke within a year. We need a vendor who owns the fix, not just the install.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Benjamin, the pattern is clear. We age systems in place, then outsource the repair and inherit the mess.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: So we need a vendor who stays through the rollout, not just a training session.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: Agreed. If the vendor isn't on-site during the peak season, we're doomed. The yard can't wait for remote support.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, your aging systems point matches my recurring costs. We need a model that doesn't bleed money after the initial approval.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: @Benjamin, your aging systems point matches my recurring costs. We need a model that doesn't bleed money after the initial approval.""}]}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, exactly. We need a single throat to choke when things break, not four suppliers pointing fingers.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, precisely. We need a model that doesn't quietly age into a liability. The 2018 lift proves external fixes often fail.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
